From 7160220e79973d6a27e4ef2e515a3ccb54251ba2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:02:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nak: rematerialization and per-shader occupancy targets
 (NAK_OCC_TARGET)

On by default; NAK_OCC_TARGET=0 turns both off.

Rematerialization (spill_remat.rs): when spilling GPRs, a value whose
definition is cheap and side-effect free (copies, integer/float ALU ops,
conversions, invariant system values, cbuf loads, global loads from
constant memory, one 32-bit component of a vector load) and whose inputs
are available wherever it is live (immediates, bound cbufs, scalar UGPRs
whose live range covers it, or other such values recomputed first, up to 3
levels and 4 instructions) is evicted without a store and recomputed at
each reload.  Inputs still resident at the reload point are used instead
of being recomputed.  A reload that needs a temporary register makes room
for it in the spiller.

Constant-memory loads whose 64-bit address is two words of a bound
constant buffer (vkd3d-proton's root CBVs) reload with a single
LDG [rZ + UR]: the address is loaded once into a pinned UGPR pair at the
start of the uniform entry block and shared by every reload from it, when
the UGPR file has room for it across the whole shader.

The spiller's eviction choice becomes next-use distance per restore cost,
values not used in the current loop first, and merge blocks no longer
refill rematerializable values on incoming edges.

Occupancy target (occ_target.rs): after pre-RA scheduling, the shader's
occupancy is computed with the workgroup and shared memory limits; for
each lower register count that gives more warps, a dry run of the spiller
estimates the loop-weighted cost and the memory spills and fills it needs.
A count that needs more than 4 memory spills/fills, or any inside a loop,
is never chosen; of the others, the one with the best estimated gain
sqrt(min(warps', 32) / min(warps, 32)) / (1 + cost / work), if at least
1.05, is scheduled for and spilled to.  NAK_GPR_CAP overrides it per
stage.  NAK_OCC_TRACE=1 prints the estimates.

Unit tests cover a constant-load component reloaded through a UGPR or a
recomputed address, a chain with a resident input, and UGPR coverage.

NAK_OCC_TARGET is part of nak_gpr_cap_key (bit 24) and so of the shader
cache keys.  With NAK_OCC_TARGET=0, output is the same as without this
patch.
